{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1523 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0a1bab0da8224e0e46a1ff06b697f72d84eb802174ede7c85bb7ff585b77d4d7" :edb/db-before-t 1522 :edb/db-after-t 1523 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534835 50 #inst "2026-10-08T08:31:24.158Z" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059522 1100 "Given that $3+2\\textrm{i} = a + \\textrm{i}b$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186059522 1100 "Given that $3+2\\textrm{i} = a + \\textrm{i}b,$ calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059522 1145 "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n3 = a\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n2 = b\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=2.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059522 1145 "First, we equate the real parts:\n$3 = a$\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n$2 = b$\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=2$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186059524 1100 "Given that $2 - 3 \\textrm{i} = \\dfrac{p - 2q \\textrm{i} }{1 + 2 \\textrm{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059524 1100 "Given that $2 - 3 \\textrm{i} = \\dfrac{p - 2q \\textrm{i}}{1 + 2 \\textrm{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186059524 1145 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1+2\\textrm{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 - 3\\textrm{i} &= \\frac{p - 2q\\textrm{i}}{1 + 2\\textrm{i}} \\\\\n(2 - 3\\textrm{i})(1 + 2\\textrm{i}) &= p - 2q\\textrm{i} \\\\\n2 + 4\\textrm{i} - 3\\textrm{i} - 6\\textrm{i}^{2} &= p - 2q\\textrm{i} \\\\\n2 + \\textrm{i} - 6(-1) &= p - 2q\\textrm{i} \\\\\n8 + \\textrm{i} &= p - 2q\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n$8 = p$.\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n$1|=-2q; q|=-\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and\n\n$$\nq = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$" 13194139534835 false] [17592186059524 1145 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1+2\\textrm{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & =\\frac{p-2q\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ (2-3\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i}-3\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}-6(-1) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 8+\\text{i} & =p-2q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8 = p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2q \\\\ q & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059525 1100 "Given that $3+5\\textrm{i} = (p+\\textrm{i}q)(1+\\textrm{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186059525 1100 "Given that $3+5\\textrm{i} = (p+\\textrm{i}q)(1+\\textrm{i}),$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059525 1145 "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $1+\\textrm{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3 + 5\\textrm{i} &= (p + \\textrm{i}q)(1 + \\textrm{i}) \\\\\n\\frac{3 + 5\\textrm{i}}{1 + \\textrm{i}} &= p + \\textrm{i}q\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((3 + 5\\textrm{i})(1 - \\textrm{i}))/((1 + \\textrm{i})(1 - \\textrm{i})) &= p + \\textrm{i}q \\\\\n\\frac{3 - 3\\textrm{i} + 5\\textrm{i} - 5\\textrm{i}^{2}}{1^{2} - \\textrm{i}^{2}} &= p + \\textrm{i}q \\\\\n(3 + 2\\textrm{i} - 5(-1))/(1 - (-1)) &= p + \\textrm{i}q \\\\\n\\frac{8 + 2\\textrm{i}}{2} &= p + \\textrm{i}q \\\\\n4 + \\textrm{i} &= p + \\textrm{i}q\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $4=p$.\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q$.\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=1$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186059525 1145 "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $1+\\textrm{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(1+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{3+5\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+2\\text{i}-5(-1)}{1-(-1)} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{8+2\\text{i}}{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $4=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=1.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186059724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313446 13194139534835 true] [17592186059724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313493 13194139534835 true] [17592186059724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313499 13194139534835 true] [17592186059724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313504 13194139534835 true] [17592186059724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313511 13194139534835 true] [17592186059726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313453 13194139534835 true] [17592186059726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313474 13194139534835 true] [17592186059726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313481 13194139534835 true] [17592186059726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313524 13194139534835 true] [17592186059726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313531 13194139534835 true] [17592186059727 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313460 13194139534835 true] [17592186059727 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313467 13194139534835 true] [17592186059727 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313487 13194139534835 true] [17592186060333 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534835 true] [17592186060333 1100 "Given that $5 - \\textrm{i} = (p + \\textrm{i}q)(3 + 2\\textrm{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186060333 1100 "Given that $5-\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186060333 1145 "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5-\\text{i}}{3+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5-\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})}{(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{15-3\\text{i}-10\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{9+4} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=1$ and $q=-1.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186060351 1017 #edb/ref 17592186059089 13194139534835 false] [17592186060351 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313518 13194139534835 true] [17592186060351 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534835 true] [17592186060351 1100 "Given that $\\frac{13\\textrm{i}}{2 - 3\\textrm{i}} = p + \\textrm{i}q$, calculate $p$ and $q$." 13194139534835 false] [17592186060351 1100 "Given that $\\frac{13\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=p+\\text{i}q,$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186060351 1145 "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2-3\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\text{i}(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 2\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -3+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-3=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $2=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3$ and $q=2.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313446 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313447 13194139534835 true] [17592186313446 1089 "q-160013" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313446 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534835 true] [17592186313446 1100 "Given that $\\frac{3}{4}+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313446 1113 #uuid "78111624-f670-5df8-b6e2-bb5a5dde19ff" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313446 1145 "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\frac{3}{4}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313448 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313449 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313450 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313451 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313452 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1041 "selection" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313452 13194139534835 true] [17592186313447 1110 #uuid "441caaff-8709-5b6c-b57d-974573fa490f" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313448 1034 "a=\\frac{3}{4},b=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534835 true] [17592186313448 1111 #uuid "d201c5d2-33ed-5990-b470-be15c705c915" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313449 1034 "a=\\sqrt{3},b=-\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534835 true] [17592186313449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534835 true] 